# 1 Carat Lab Grown Marquise Diamond ({{year}}): 3 Grades Under $1,000

![Three 1 carat marquise cut lab grown diamonds in jeweler tweezers against a grey backdrop with text overlay reading 1 Carat Lab Marquise Diamond 3 Grades Under 1000 as the DiamondCritics featured image for the 1 carat lab grown marquise diamond guide](/images/1-carat-lab-marquise-diamond.jpg "1 Carat Lab Marquise Diamond 3 Grades Under 1000")

## TL;DR — 1 Carat Lab Marquise in One Scroll

**A 1 carat lab grown marquise diamond is a chemically identical stone to a mined 1ct marquise — same carbon, same hardness, same brilliance.** The price is not the same.

**The 3 IGI-certified grades under $1,000:**
- **Grade 1 — E-VVS2 Excellent at $629:** Entry floor. 79% below a natural G-VS2 equivalent (~$3,000).
- **Grade 2 — E-VVS1 Excellent at $886:** Best value step-up. Near-flawless clarity for under $900.
- **Grade 3 — D-VVS1 Ideal at $958:** Top colour + near-flawless clarity. Under $1,000. Natural D-VVS1 costs $6,000+.

**Also under $1,000:** D-VVS2 Excellent at $657 — top colour, one clarity step below VVS1.

→ Entry pick: **[IGI 1ct E-VVS2 Excellent at $629](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29389739?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**
→ Mid pick: **[IGI 1ct E-VVS1 Excellent at $886](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29517802?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**
→ Top pick: **[IGI 1ct D-VVS1 Ideal at $958](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29978545?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

**Priority:** All 3 grades are IGI-certified, eye-clean, and cut for the marquise shape. The step from $629 to $958 moves you from E-VVS2 to D-VVS1 — a full two-clarity-grade and one-colour-grade jump for $329 more. See the full [marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond) for shape fundamentals.

## Expert Summary

Certified 1ct lab grown marquise inventory runs from **$629** to **$1,381**. Three grades stay under $1,000: E-VVS2 at $629, E-VVS1 at $886, D-VVS1 at $958. A natural 1ct G-VS2 marquise costs ~$3,000. The lab entry at $629 saves 79%.

I'm Farzana Hasan, a diamond expert. At 1ct, the difference between E-VVS2 and D-VVS1 is invisible on the finger. Both are eye-clean. Both read brilliant white in a white metal setting. The $329 gap is about the certificate, not the look. My recommendation: start at E-VVS2. Look at the 360° video. Only step up if the certificate grade matters to you. Full credentials at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**. Our pillar **[marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond)** covers every marquise topic.

This guide covers the Sub-$1,000 Grade Stack, the VVS1 Value Ceiling, and the D-vs-E False Economy. It includes grade-by-grade pricing with specific certified stones, the above-$1,000 tier, and setting pairing. All prices verified against live certified market data.

