## The Sub-$1,000 Grade Stack

**The Sub-$1,000 Grade Stack is the specific sequence of IGI-certified grade combinations that keep a 1ct lab grown marquise diamond under $1,000.** Not every combination stays under $1,000. Knowing which three do maps your full value range before you start shopping.

Here is the stack in order:

**Stack Level 1 — E-VVS2 at $629.** E colour is one grade below D on the GIA colour scale. VVS2 clarity means inclusions are not visible under 10x magnification without deliberate effort. This stone is eye-clean from any normal viewing distance. It grades above what most natural 1ct budgets can reach. Natural G-VS2 at ~$3,000 is a lower grade. The lab stone at $629 is a better stone on paper and costs 79% less.

**Stack Level 2 — E-VVS1 at $886.** The step from VVS2 to VVS1 adds $257. VVS1 means inclusions are extremely difficult to find even under 10x magnification. Visually, VVS1 and VVS2 look identical — the difference exists only on the certificate. The certificate matters for resale and for anyone who wants the cleanest possible grade documentation on their stone.

**Stack Level 3 — D-VVS1 at $958.** The step from E-VVS1 to D-VVS1 adds $72. D colour is the absolute top of the GIA colour scale — colourless. The colour difference between D and E is invisible to the naked eye under any normal viewing conditions. D reads as a stronger certificate and is the max colour grade available. At $958, this is the highest-quality certified 1ct lab marquise you can buy for under $1,000.

