## Grade 2 — E-VVS1 at $886 (Mid Pick)

The E-VVS1 is the mid-tier of the Sub-$1,000 Grade Stack. Six stones available from $886 to $929. All IGI-certified. Excellent and Ideal cut grades.

**What changes from Grade 1 to Grade 2:** One clarity step — VVS2 to VVS1. That's it. The colour stays E. The stone still looks identical on the finger. The certificate reads more cleanly. VVS1 means inclusions are extremely difficult to find under 10x — even harder than VVS2. No change in face-up appearance, no change in brilliance, no change in the ring as it looks on your hand.

**The $257 premium explained:** VVS1 stones are rarer than VVS2 in natural diamonds. Lab production replicates this grading scarcity slightly — VVS1 stones command a modest premium even in lab because fewer stones reach that grade threshold. The $257 gap between E-VVS2 and E-VVS1 reflects that rarity premium, not a visual quality difference.

**When to choose E-VVS1:** You want the cleaner certificate for documentation. You're buying as a gift and the grade reads better on paper. You're planning to pass the ring down and want the strongest mid-tier cert. You have the budget and simply prefer VVS1.

