## Grade 3 — D-VVS1 at $958 (Top Under-$1,000 Pick)

The D-VVS1 Ideal is the peak of the Sub-$1,000 Grade Stack. Two stones at $958. Both IGI-certified. Both Ideal cut.

**What you get at $958:** D colour (the absolute maximum — completely colourless), VVS1 clarity (near-flawless), Ideal cut (the top cut grade on the IGI scale). This is the strongest certified 1ct lab marquise available for under $1,000. Natural D-VVS1 1ct marquise costs $6,000+. The lab stone saves 84%.

**The $72 gap from E-VVS1 to D-VVS1:** colour grade E→D. That's the only change. VVS1 stays the same. Cut stays Ideal. On the finger, in any setting, under any normal light — D and E look the same. The $72 buys the D on the certificate. That is a legitimate purchase if the certificate matters to you.

**When to choose D-VVS1:** You want the maximum certificate for under $1,000. You're setting in platinum and want the strongest white-metal + white-stone pairing on paper. You plan to pass the stone down and want the most credible documentation. The $42 remaining budget ($1,000 − $958) goes toward a better setting.

