**Verdict:** Pay $1,381 only if the IF or FL certificate matters to you specifically. For a 1ct stone you'll wear in a ring, D-VVS1 at $958 is the rational ceiling. The $423 you save vs D-IF is better spent on a better setting or a larger stone.

## Setting Pairing for 1ct Lab Grown Marquise

A 1ct lab marquise measures approximately 10x5mm face-up. It fits every standard marquise setting. The setting choice matters more for this shape than for any round. Marquise tips are the most vulnerable points.

**Six-prong solitaire for daily wear.** Two prongs at each tip plus two at the sides give full tip coverage. A six-prong solitaire from $1,355 in white gold is the default recommendation for a 1ct lab marquise worn every day. Total ring cost with E-VVS2 at $629: under $2,100.

**Petite pavé for a shoulder sparkle.** The petite pavé solitaire from $1,895 adds shoulder stones without overwhelming a 1ct centre. The 1ct marquise reads cleanly at centre with pavé framing. Total ring with E-VVS2: under $2,600.

**Bezel for active wear.** The Comfort Fit Bezel at $1,250 fully wraps both tips. Zero tip-chip risk. Trade-off: slightly reduced side brilliance from the metal lip. Total ring with E-VVS2: under $1,900. See our [marquise bezel engagement ring guide](/marquise-bezel-engagement-ring).

**Metal pairing:** D-E colour lab stones look best in platinum or white gold — the cool metal amplifies the stone's colourless appearance. In yellow or rose gold, step down to G colour and save $150 vs E. See our [white gold marquise engagement ring guide](/white-gold-marquise-engagement-ring) and [platinum marquise engagement ring guide](/platinum-marquise-engagement-ring) for the full setting selection at every price.

